  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Minimalist Design**\n\nI\'m exploring how to execute this request for a stark white website. Currently, my focus is on removing any unnecessary UI elements or HUD. I\'m examining the React component provided, starting to dissect it for potential minimalist modifications and streamlined functionality for the target audience.\n\n\n**Analyzing Component Structure**\n\nNow I\'m diving deeper into the styling, specifically the Card component. I\'m focusing on the box-shadows and pseudo-elements, evaluating if these effects can be simplified or eliminated to achieve the minimalist aesthetic. I\'m also planning the modifications to the component, so that it will render according to the target audience\'s needs.\n\n\n**Evaluating CSS Implementation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the CSS implementation of the water droplet effect. The user wants a pure white background without any UI elements, so I\'m focusing on crafting a realistic droplet using either `src/index.css`, Tailwind, inline styles, or a separate CSS file. I will check the existing libraries to streamline this effort. I\'m prioritizing minimal dependencies and elegant styling to meet the specified minimalist requirement.\n\n\n**Optimizing CSS Placement**\n\nI\'m now determining the most effective location for the CSS classes, and I\'m finding that putting `.card`, `.card::after`, and `.card::before` directly into `src/index.css` or component styling would allow pixel-perfect rendering, eliminating the need for `styled-components` entirely. I\'m focusing on the \"totally white site\" container and centering it with `bg-white min-h-screen w-full flex items-center justify-center m-0 p-0 overflow-hidden` for a clean, minimalist design with the droplet centered.\n\n\n**Refining UI Constraints**\n\nI\'ve just revisited the core requirements: a stark white site with *no* extraneous UI. This means *literally* nothing except the centered droplet. I\'m exploring subtle interactivity \342\200\223 hover, drag, or floating \342\200\223 but the priority is fidelity to the existing code snippet, perfectly centered on a white background. The focus is on ensuring the droplet renders as a realistic 3D drop on the pure white surface, so it looks like it sits on a white surface. The challenge is balancing the realism of the drop with the minimalist requirement.\n\n\n"
