  planner_response {
    response: "I have made the water droplet fully dynamic with authentic liquid physics and recoil on the clean, pure white canvas:\n\n- **Dynamic Droplet Deformation**:\n  - **Bottom Impact & Resting Shape**: When the droplet drops to the bottom, it squashes on impact and flattens against the floor\342\200\224its bottom border radius morphs from rounded curves into a flattened bead, spreading wider horizontally like real water.\n  - **In-Flight Velocity Stretch**: When moving fast or thrown through the air, the droplet elongates along its velocity vector.\n  - **Harmonic Surface Tension Wobble**: High-frequency spring-damper recoil oscillates on collision and naturally dampens out.\n- **Fluid Drag & Throw Mechanics**:\n  - Drag the droplet anywhere across the screen.\n  - Fling / throw it in any direction with realistic momentum.\n  - It bounces off all four edges of the screen, squashes perpendicularly against each wall, and recoils dynamically.\n- **Pure Canvas**:\n  - Retains the completely white background (`#ffffff`) with zero menus, HUD, or extra UI elements."
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Requirements**\n\nI\'m focusing on the user\'s explicit needs: a completely white interface, devoid of any UI elements, HUD, text, or telemetry. The crucial element is achieving dynamic, water-like responsiveness and the ability to alter its shape, echoing the metaphor of a water droplet. The challenge lies in making it dynamic.\n\n\n"
