  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Squash and Stretch**\n\nI\'m currently focused on `src/App.tsx`, specifically the squash and stretch animation. I\'ve been aiming for a gentler effect, limiting the scale to between 0.86 and 1.18. I\'m also exploring wobble. My goal is to prevent overly dramatic recoil while maintaining a pleasing visual impact.\n\n\n**Adjusting Collision Dynamics**\n\nI\'ve significantly softened the collision impulses by introducing higher spring damping (`SPRING_DAMP = 14`, `SPRING_K = 110`) and reduced restitution values. The squash multiplier is now around 0.0009, with a hard cap, and air drag is at 0.985. Velocity stretch is capped at 0.18, and border radius perturbations are subtle at \302\2614%.\n\n\n**Designing App Docking Behavior**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the app docking behavior. I envision a seamless transition, starting with the app nestled within the taskbar. Upon user interaction, the droplet will smoothly detach and deform, as if extruded from the taskbar itself, expanding into a full-fledged app window. The \"water-taskbar\" glass effect is crucial, and a glowing indicator dot will signal app activity.\n\n\n**Developing Liquid Pinch-Off**\n\nI\'m currently working to establish the liquid bridge connecting the taskbar bead and the emerging droplet. I\'m focusing on the Y-axis stretch (scaleY: 1.35, scaleX: 0.72) to simulate surface tension. The pinch-off should occur cleanly at roughly 90px above the taskbar. I\'m then considering the droplet\'s smooth arc and expansion (from 0.2 to 1.0) into the full app window, aiming for silky oscillations during the settling state.\n\n\n**Visualizing Fluid Meniscus**\n\nI\'m now implementing the liquid meniscus calculation and rendering, focusing on a jaw-dropping organic separation effect. I\'m leveraging tangent points or quadratic Bezier curves for the SVG path generation, ensuring the water shading (inset shadows, white highlights) creates a realistic connection between the docked app and the emerging droplet. The bridge is calculated based on distance, radii, and a `bridgeRatio`.\n\nThe extrusion timing and easing are also being reviewed. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the Y-axis stretch (scaleY: 1.35, scaleX: 0.72) from `p = 0` to `p = 0.45` to simulate surface tension. The droplet\'s movement is capped at 80px, and the liquid bridge visibly thins as the droplet expands.\n\n\n**Orchestrating Transition Sequences**\n\nI\'m now refining the docking and undocking animations, concentrating on smooth transitions. The bridge now snaps at `p = 0.45` with a soft jiggle, and the droplet smoothly moves to the screen center with expansion and settled stretch. I\'ve also incorporated the docking animation; a flying, stretching, shrinking droplet merges with the taskbar, creating the docking state. Inside the 1:1 window, I\'m aiming for a minimalist, clean droplet experience, including a digital droplet clock.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_50657"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"/**\\n * @license\\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\\n */\\n\\nimport { useEffect, useRef, useState, useCallback } from \'react\';\\n\\ninterface PointerHistory {\\n  x: number;\\n  y: number;\\n  time: number;\\n}\\n\\ntype AppWindowStatus = \'docked\' | \'extruding\' | \'floating\' | \'docking\';\\n\\nexport default function App() {\\n  const cardRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\\n  const taskbarBeadRef = useRef<HTMLButtonElement>(null);\\n  const bridgeCanvasRef = useRef<SVGSVGElement>(null);\\n\\n  // App window state: \'docked\' (inside taskbar), \'extruding\' (budding out), \'floating\' (active), \'docking\' (merging back)\\n  const [appStatus, setAppStatus] = useState<AppWindowStatus>(\'docked\');\\n  const [currentTime, setCurrentTime] = useState(\'\');\\n  const [ripples, setRipples] = useState<{ id: number; x: number; y: number }[]>([]);\\n\\n  // Update time for the 1:1 app clock\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const updateTime = () => {\\n      const d = new Date();\\n      setCurrentTime(\\n        d.toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: \'2-digit\', minute: \'2-digit\' })\\n      );\\n    };\\n    updateTime();\\n    const interval = setInterval(updateTime, 1000);\\n    return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Physics and animation state in refs\\n  const stateRef = useRef({\\n    status: \'docked\' as AppWindowStatus,\\n    // Droplet position (center)\\n    x: 0,\\n    y: 0,\\n    vx: 0,\\n    vy: 0,\\n\\n    // Controlled, subtle liquid wobble & recoil\\n    wobbleX: 0,\\n    wobbleY: 0,\\n    wobbleVelX: 0,\\n    wobbleVelY: 0,\\n\\n    // Taskbar icon anchor coordinates\\n    dockX: 0,\\n    dockY: 0,\\n\\n    // Transition progress & start coords\\n    transStartTime: 0,\\n    transStartX: 0,\\n    transStartY: 0,\\n    transTargetX: 0,\\n    transTargetY: 0,\\n\\n    // Drag interaction\\n    isDragging: false,\\n    dragPointerId: -1,\\n    dragOffsetX: 0,\\n    dragOffsetY: 0,\\n    targetX: 0,\\n    targetY: 0,\\n    history: [] as PointerHistory[],\\n\\n    lastTime: 0,\\n  });\\n\\n  // Calculate taskbar bead position\\n  const updateDockCoords = useCallback(() => {\\n    if (taskbarBeadRef.current) {\\n      const rect = taskbarBeadRef.current.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      stateRef.current.dockX = rect.left + rect.width / 2;\\n      stateRef.current.dockY = rect.top + rect.height / 2;\\n    }\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    updateDockCoords();\\n    window.addEventListener(\'resize\', updateDockCoords);\\n    return () => window.removeEventListener(\'resize\', updateDockCoords);\\n  }, [updateDockCoords]);\\n\\n  // Launch / Extrude the 1:1 droplet app from the taskbar\\n  const launchApp = useCallback(() => {\\n    updateDockCoords();\\n    const state = stateRef.current;\\n    if (state.status === \'extruding\' || state.status === \'docking\') return;\\n\\n    if (state.status === \'floating\') {\\n      // If already open, dock it back\\n      dockApp();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Begin liquid extrusion\\n    state.status = \'extruding\';\\n    setAppStatus(\'extruding\');\\n    state.transStartTime = performance.now();\\n    state.transStartX = state.dockX;\\n    state.transStartY = state.dockY;\\n    state.transTargetX = window.innerWidth / 2;\\n    state.transTargetY = Math.max(160, window.innerHeight * 0.42);\\n\\n    state.x = state.dockX;\\n    state.y = state.dockY;\\n    state.vx = 0;\\n    state.vy = -200;\\n    state.wobbleX = 0;\\n    state.wobbleY = 0;\\n    state.wobbleVelX = 0;\\n    state.wobbleVelY = 0;\\n  }, [updateDockCoords]);\\n\\n  // Dock / Absorb the 1:1 droplet app back into the taskbar\\n  const dockApp = useCallback(() => {\\n    updateDockCoords();\\n    const state = stateRef.current;\\n    if (state.status === \'docked\' || state.status === \'docking\') return;\\n\\n    state.status = \'docking\';\\n    setAppStatus(\'docking\');\\n    state.isDragging = false;\\n    state.transStartTime = performance.now();\\n    state.transStartX = state.x;\\n    state.transStartY = state.y;\\n    state.transTargetX = state.dockX;\\n    state.transTargetY = state.dockY;\\n    state.vx = 0;\\n    state.vy = 0;\\n  }, [updateDockCoords]);\\n\\n  // Main 60-120fps Animation & Physics Loop\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    let animId: number;\\n\\n    const R = 95; // Effective radius for 220px 1:1 window\\n    const GRAVITY = 750; // Gentle downward gravity\\n    const AIR_RESISTANCE = 0.985; // Subtle air drag\\n    const BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_BOTTOM = 0.28; // Calmed recoil: settles softly\\n    const BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_WALL = 0.35; // Calmed wall bounce: soft liquid absorption\\n    const SPRING_K = 110; // Surface tension spring recovery\\n    const SPRING_DAMP = 14; // High fluid viscosity damping: no over-deformation!\\n\\n    const loop = (timestamp: number) => {\\n      const state = stateRef.current;\\n      if (!state.lastTime) state.lastTime = timestamp;\\n      const dt = Math.min((timestamp - state.lastTime) / 1000, 0.033);\\n      state.lastTime = timestamp;\\n\\n      const screenW = window.innerWidth;\\n      const screenH = window.innerHeight;\\n\\n      // Available bounding area (above taskbar)\\n      const taskbarTop = state.dockY - 35;\\n      const minX = R + 10;\\n      const maxX = screenW - R - 10;\\n      const minY = R + 10;\\n      const maxY = Math.min(screenH - R - 10, taskbarTop - 15);\\n\\n      let currentScale = 1;\\n      let bridgeOpacity = 0;\\n      let bridgePath = \'\';\\n\\n      // 1. Extruding transition (budding from taskbar)\\n      if (state.status === \'extruding\') {\\n        const elapsed = (timestamp - state.transStartTime) / 1000;\\n        const duration = 0.75;\\n        const progress = Math.min(1, elapsed / duration);\\n\\n        // Smooth cubic ease out\\n        const easeOut = 1 - Math.pow(1 - progress, 3);\\n        const easeIn = Math.pow(progress, 2);\\n\\n        // Position interpolation\\n        state.x = state.transStartX + (state.transTargetX - state.transStartX) * easeOut;\\n        state.y = state.transStartY + (state.transTargetY - state.transStartY) * easeOut;\\n\\n        // In phase 1 (0 to 0.4): droplet stretches upward out of the taskbar with liquid neck\\n        if (progress < 0.42) {\\n          const stretchPhase = progress / 0.42;\\n          currentScale = 0.22 + stretchPhase * 0.35;\\n          // Stretches along Y, compresses along X (liquid meniscus pulling free)\\n          state.wobbleY = 0.28 * Math.sin(stretchPhase * Math.PI);\\n          state.wobbleX = -0.16 * Math.sin(stretchPhase * Math.PI);\\n\\n          // Liquid bridge drawing between taskbar bead and emerging drop\\n          bridgeOpacity = Math.max(0, 1 - stretchPhase * 0.9);\\n          const neckRadiusDock = 22 * (1 - stretchPhase * 0.4);\\n          const neckRadiusDrop = 14 + stretchPhase * 16;\\n          const pinchWidth = Math.max(4, 18 * (1 - stretchPhase * 0.85));\\n\\n          const midY = (state.dockY + state.y) / 2;\\n          bridgePath = `\\n            M ${state.dockX - neckRadiusDock} ${state.dockY}\\n            Q ${state.dockX - pinchWidth} ${midY}, ${state.x - neckRadiusDrop} ${state.y}\\n            L ${state.x + neckRadiusDrop} ${state.y}\\n            Q ${state.dockX + pinchWidth} ${midY}, ${state.dockX + neckRadiusDock} ${state.dockY}\\n            Z\\n          `;\\n        } else {\\n          // Phase 2: Neck has snapped! Droplet blooms smoothly into full 1:1 window\\n          const bloomPhase = (progress - 0.42) / 0.58;\\n          currentScale = 0.57 + 0.43 * (1 - Math.pow(1 - bloomPhase, 2));\\n\\n          // Gentle liquid recoil jiggle upon pinch-off\\n          state.wobbleY = 0.12 * Math.cos(bloomPhase * Math.PI * 3) * (1 - bloomPhase);\\n          state.wobbleX = -0.08 * Math.cos(bloomPhase * Math.PI * 3) * (1 - bloomPhase);\\n          bridgeOpacity = 0;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (progress >= 1) {\\n          state.status = \'floating\';\\n          setAppStatus(\'floating\');\\n          state.vx = 0;\\n          state.vy = 0;\\n          state.wobbleX = 0;\\n          state.wobbleY = 0;\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      // 2. Docking transition (merging back into taskbar)\\n      else if (state.status === \'docking\') {\\n        const elapsed = (timestamp - state.transStartTime) / 1000;\\n        const duration = 0.55;\\n        const progress = Math.min(1, elapsed / duration);\\n\\n        const easeIn = Math.pow(progress, 2.5);\\n        state.x = state.transStartX + (state.transTargetX - state.transStartX) * easeIn;\\n        state.y = state.transStartY + (state.transTargetY - state.transStartY) * easeIn;\\n\\n        // Shrinks down towards taskbar bead\\n        currentScale = Math.max(0.2, 1 - easeIn * 0.8);\\n\\n        // Droplet elongates towards destination\\n        state.wobbleY = 0.22 * Math.sin(progress * Math.PI);\\n        state.wobbleX = -0.12 * Math.sin(progress * Math.PI);\\n\\n        // Near the end, liquid bridge forms to absorb the drop\\n        if (progress > 0.6) {\\n          const absorbPhase = (progress - 0.6) / 0.4;\\n          bridgeOpacity = absorbPhase;\\n          const pinchWidth = 14 * absorbPhase;\\n          const midY = (state.dockY + state.y) / 2;\\n          bridgePath = `\\n            M ${state.dockX - 20} ${state.dockY}\\n            Q ${state.dockX - pinchWidth} ${midY}, ${state.x - 14} ${state.y}\\n            L ${state.x + 14} ${state.y}\\n            Q ${state.dockX + pinchWidth} ${midY}, ${state.dockX + 20} ${state.dockY}\\n            Z\\n          `;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (progress >= 1) {\\n          state.status = \'docked\';\\n          setAppStatus(\'docked\');\\n          bridgeOpacity = 0;\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      // 3. Floating Interactive State (with calmed, refined deformation & recoil)\\n      else if (state.status === \'floating\') {\\n        currentScale = 1;\\n\\n        if (state.isDragging) {\\n          // Smooth fluid tracking to pointer\\n          const followSpeed = 30;\\n          const dx = state.targetX - state.x;\\n          const dy = state.targetY - state.y;\\n\\n          state.vx = dx * followSpeed;\\n          state.vy = dy * followSpeed;\\n\\n          state.x += dx * Math.min(1, followSpeed * dt);\\n          state.y += dy * Math.min(1, followSpeed * dt);\\n\\n          // Bounds clamp while dragging\\n          state.x = Math.max(minX, Math.min(maxX, state.x));\\n          state.y = Math.max(minY, Math.min(maxY, state.y));\\n\\n          // Calmed drag stretch: restrained to max 0.12 so it never deforms too much\\n          const dragSpeed = Math.hypot(state.vx, state.vy);\\n          if (dragSpeed > 80) {\\n            const dragStretch = Math.min(dragSpeed * 0.00012, 0.12);\\n            const angle = Math.atan2(state.vy, state.vx);\\n            state.wobbleX += (Math.cos(angle) * dragStretch - state.wobbleX) * 0.1;\\n            state.wobbleY += (Math.sin(angle) * dragStretch - state.wobbleY) * 0.1;\\n          }\\n        } else {\\n          // Gravity\\n          state.vy += GRAVITY * dt;\\n\\n          // Air resistance\\n          state.vx *= Math.pow(AIR_RESISTANCE, dt * 60);\\n          state.vy *= Math.pow(AIR_RESISTANCE, dt * 60);\\n\\n          state.x += state.vx * dt;\\n          state.y += state.vy * dt;\\n\\n          // Collision with floor (resting area above taskbar)\\n          if (state.y >= maxY) {\\n            state.y = maxY;\\n            const impactSpeed = state.vy;\\n\\n            if (impactSpeed > 40) {\\n              // Gentle, refined squash: strictly clamped\\n              const squashPower = Math.min(impactSpeed * 0.0008, 0.25);\\n              state.wobbleVelY -= squashPower * 8;\\n              state.wobbleVelX += squashPower * 6;\\n              state.vy = -impactSpeed * BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_BOTTOM;\\n            } else {\\n              state.vy = 0;\\n              // Ground friction\\n              state.vx *= Math.pow(0.85, dt * 60);\\n              if (Math.abs(state.vx) < 3) state.vx = 0;\\n            }\\n          }\\n\\n          // Collision with ceiling\\n          if (state.y <= minY) {\\n            state.y = minY;\\n            const impactSpeed = Math.abs(state.vy);\\n            if (impactSpeed > 40) {\\n              const squashPower = Math.min(impactSpeed * 0.0008, 0.22);\\n              state.wobbleVelY += squashPower * 6;\\n              state.wobbleVelX -= squashPower * 5;\\n            }\\n            state.vy = Math.abs(state.vy) * BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_WALL;\\n          }\\n\\n          // Collision with left wall (recoil)\\n          if (state.x <= minX) {\\n            state.x = minX;\\n            const impactSpeed = Math.abs(state.vx);\\n            if (impactSpeed > 35) {\\n              const squashPower = Math.min(impactSpeed * 0.0009, 0.24);\\n              state.wobbleVelX += squashPower * 7;\\n              state.wobbleVelY -= squashPower * 5;\\n            }\\n            state.vx = Math.abs(state.vx) * BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_WALL;\\n          }\\n\\n          // Collision with right wall (recoil)\\n          if (state.x >= maxX) {\\n            state.x = maxX;\\n            const impactSpeed = Math.abs(state.vx);\\n            if (impactSpeed > 35) {\\n              const squashPower = Math.min(impactSpeed * 0.0009, 0.24);\\n              state.wobbleVelX += squashPower * 7;\\n              state.wobbleVelY -= squashPower * 5;\\n            }\\n            state.vx = -Math.abs(state.vx) * BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_WALL;\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Wobble spring damper simulation (strictly clamped)\\n        const accX = -SPRING_K * state.wobbleX - SPRING_DAMP * state.wobbleVelX;\\n        const accY = -SPRING_K * state.wobbleY - SPRING_DAMP * state.wobbleVelY;\\n        state.wobbleVelX += accX * dt;\\n        state.wobbleVelY += accY * dt;\\n        state.wobbleX += state.wobbleVelX * dt;\\n        state.wobbleY += state.wobbleVelY * dt;\\n\\n        // Hard clamp wobble displacement so it NEVER over-deforms!\\n        state.wobbleX = Math.max(-0.14, Math.min(0.14, state.wobbleX));\\n        state.wobbleY = Math.max(-0.14, Math.min(0.14, state.wobbleY));\\n      }\\n\\n      // Render bridge canvas if extruding or docking\\n      if (bridgeCanvasRef.current) {\\n        const pathEl = bridgeCanvasRef.current.querySelector(\'path\');\\n        if (pathEl) {\\n          pathEl.setAttribute(\'d\', bridgePath);\\n          bridgeCanvasRef.current.style.opacity = bridgeOpacity.toString();\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      // Render 1:1 Window\\n      if (cardRef.current) {\\n        if (state.status === \'docked\') {\\n          cardRef.current.style.display = \'none\';\\n        } else {\\n          cardRef.current.style.display = \'flex\';\\n\\n          // Controlled scale: clamp strictly between 0.86 and 1.18\\n          const bottomDistance = Math.max(0, maxY - state.y);\\n          const bottomProximity = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, 1 - bottomDistance / 50));\\n          const bottomFlattenX = bottomProximity * 0.08;\\n          const bottomFlattenY = -bottomProximity * 0.06;\\n\\n          const rawScaleX = (1 + state.wobbleX + bottomFlattenX) * currentScale;\\n          const rawScaleY = (1 + state.wobbleY + bottomFlattenY) * currentScale;\\n\\n          const finalScaleX = Math.max(0.18, Math.min(1.2, rawScaleX));\\n          const finalScaleY = Math.max(0.18, Math.min(1.2, rawScaleY));\\n\\n          // Center offset: width/height is 220, anchor is -110px, -110px\\n          const tx = state.x - 110;\\n          const ty = state.y - 110;\\n\\n          cardRef.current.style.transform = `translate3d(${tx}px, ${ty}px, 0) scale(${finalScaleX}, ${finalScaleY})`;\\n\\n          // Restrained organic border-radius: variations kept strictly within \302\2615%\\n          // so it always maintains its clean water drop shape without turning weird\\n          const t = timestamp * 0.002;\\n          const breath = Math.sin(t * 2) * 1.5;\\n\\n          const tl = Math.round(51 + state.wobbleX * 6 + breath);\\n          const tr = Math.round(49 - state.wobbleX * 6 - breath);\\n          const br = Math.round(62 * (1 - bottomProximity * 0.22) + state.wobbleY * 5);\\n          const bl = Math.round(38 * (1 - bottomProximity * 0.18) - state.wobbleY * 5);\\n\\n          const vtl = Math.round(25 + bottomProximity * 12 + state.wobbleY * 6);\\n          const vtr = Math.round(57 + bottomProximity * 8 - state.wobbleY * 6);\\n          const vbr = Math.round(43 * (1 - bottomProximity * 0.25) - state.wobbleX * 4);\\n          const vbl = Math.round(75 * (1 - bottomProximity * 0.2) + state.wobbleX * 4);\\n\\n          cardRef.current.style.borderRadius = `${tl}% ${tr}% ${br}% ${bl}% / ${vtl}% ${vtr}% ${vbr}% ${vbl}%`;\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      animId = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\\n    };\\n\\n    animId = requestAnimationFrame(loop);\\n    return () => cancelAnimationFrame(animId);\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Pointer dragging handlers for the 1:1 window\\n  const handlePointerDown = (e: React.PointerEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\\n    const state = stateRef.current;\\n    if (state.status !== \'floating\') return;\\n\\n    state.isDragging = true;\\n    state.dragPointerId = e.pointerId;\\n    e.currentTarget.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\\n\\n    state.dragOffsetX = e.clientX - state.x;\\n    state.dragOffsetY = e.clientY - state.y;\\n    state.targetX = e.clientX - state.dragOffsetX;\\n    state.targetY = e.clientY - state.dragOffsetY;\\n\\n    state.history = [{ x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY, time: performance.now() }];\\n\\n    // Subtle gentle pickup squish\\n    state.wobbleVelX += 2;\\n    state.wobbleVelY -= 3;\\n  };\\n\\n  const handlePointerMove = (e: React.PointerEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\\n    const state = stateRef.current;\\n    if (!state.isDragging || state.dragPointerId !== e.pointerId) return;\\n\\n    state.targetX = e.clientX - state.dragOffsetX;\\n    state.targetY = e.clientY - state.dragOffsetY;\\n\\n    const now = performance.now();\\n    state.history.push({ x: e.clientX, y: e.clientY, time: now });\\n\\n    while (state.history.length > 2 && now - state.history[0].time > 100) {\\n      state.history.shift();\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handlePointerUp = (e: React.PointerEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\\n    const state = stateRef.current;\\n    if (!state.isDragging || state.dragPointerId !== e.pointerId) return;\\n\\n    state.isDragging = false;\\n    state.dragPointerId = -1;\\n\\n    try {\\n      e.currentTarget.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId);\\n    } catch {\\n      // Ignore\\n    }\\n\\n    // Check if dropped near the taskbar: if so, smoothly absorb and dock!\\n    const distToDock = Math.hypot(state.x - state.dockX, state.y - state.dockY);\\n    if (distToDock < 140) {\\n      dockApp();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    // Fling / throw velocity with calm limits\\n    const now = performance.now();\\n    const history = state.history.filter((h) => now - h.time <= 100);\\n\\n    if (history.length >= 2) {\\n      const oldest = history[0];\\n      const newest = history[history.length - 1];\\n      const timeDelta = (newest.time - oldest.time) / 1000;\\n\\n      if (timeDelta > 0.015) {\\n        const throwVx = (newest.x - oldest.x) / timeDelta;\\n        const throwVy = (newest.y - oldest.y) / timeDelta;\\n\\n        // Controlled speed cap: throws stay gentle, calm and elegant\\n        const maxSpeed = 1600;\\n        const speed = Math.hypot(throwVx, throwVy);\\n        if (speed > maxSpeed) {\\n          state.vx = (throwVx / speed) * maxSpeed;\\n          state.vy = (throwVy / speed) * maxSpeed;\\n        } else {\\n          state.vx = throwVx;\\n          state.vy = throwVy;\\n        }\\n\\n        if (speed > 200) {\\n          const flingSquash = Math.min(speed * 0.0003, 0.12);\\n          state.wobbleVelX += flingSquash * 3;\\n          state.wobbleVelY -= flingSquash * 3;\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  // Click inside the 1:1 window to create a water ripple\\n  const handleWindowClick = (e: React.MouseEvent<HTMLDivElement>) => {\\n    const rect = e.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect();\\n    const rippleX = e.clientX - rect.left;\\n    const rippleY = e.clientY - rect.top;\\n\\n    const newRipple = { id: Date.now(), x: rippleX, y: rippleY };\\n    setRipples((prev) => [...prev.slice(-3), newRipple]);\\n\\n    // Soft liquid jiggle on tap\\n    stateRef.current.wobbleVelY -= 4;\\n    stateRef.current.wobbleVelX += 3;\\n\\n    setTimeout(() => {\\n      setRipples((prev) => prev.filter((r) => r.id !== newRipple.id));\\n    }, 900);\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <main className=\\\"w-screen h-screen min-h-screen bg-white relative overflow-hidden m-0 p-0 select-none\\\">\\n      {/* SVG Liquid Neck / Meniscus (connects taskbar bead and emerging 1:1 window) */}\\n      <svg\\n        ref={bridgeCanvasRef}\\n        className=\\\"pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 w-full h-full z-10 transition-opacity duration-150\\\"\\n        style={{ opacity: 0 }}\\n      >\\n        <defs>\\n          <linearGradient id=\\\"waterBridgeGrad\\\" x1=\\\"0%\\\" y1=\\\"0%\\\" x2=\\\"0%\\\" y2=\\\"100%\\\">\\n            <stop offset=\\\"0%\\\" stopColor=\\\"rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9)\\\" />\\n            <stop offset=\\\"50%\\\" stopColor=\\\"rgba(235, 240, 245, 0.45)\\\" />\\n            <stop offset=\\\"100%\\\" stopColor=\\\"rgba(200, 210, 220, 0.6)\\\" />\\n          </linearGradient>\\n          <filter id=\\\"bridgeShadow\\\" x=\\\"-20%\\\" y=\\\"-20%\\\" width=\\\"140%\\\" height=\\\"140%\\\">\\n            <feDropShadow dx=\\\"2\\\" dy=\\\"4\\\" stdDeviation=\\\"4\\\" floodColor=\\\"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18)\\\" />\\n          </feDropShadow>\\n        </filter>\\n        </defs>\\n        <path\\n          d=\\\"\\\"\\n          fill=\\\"url(#waterBridgeGrad)\\\"\\n          filter=\\\"url(#bridgeShadow)\\\"\\n          stroke=\\\"rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75)\\\"\\n          strokeWidth=\\\"1.5\\\"\\n        />\\n      </svg>\\n\\n      {/* 1:1 Water Droplet App Window */}\\n      <div\\n        ref={cardRef}\\n        className=\\\"card\\\"\\n        style={{ display: \'none\' }}\\n        onPointerDown={handlePointerDown}\\n        onPointerMove={handlePointerMove}\\n        onPointerUp={handlePointerUp}\\n        onPointerCancel={handlePointerUp}\\n        onClick={handleWindowClick}\\n      >\\n        {/* Minimize bead (merges app back into taskbar) */}\\n        <button\\n          type=\\\"button\\\"\\n          aria-label=\\\"Minimize into taskbar\\\"\\n          className=\\\"minimize-bead\\\"\\n          onClick={(e) => {\\n            e.stopPropagation();\\n            dockApp();\\n          }}\\n          onPointerDown={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}\\n        />\\n\\n        {/* Minimalist 1:1 App Content */}\\n        <div className=\\\"relative z-10 pointer-events-none flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-1 select-none w-full h-full p-4\\\">\\n          {/* Subtle water droplet icon indicator */}\\n          <div className=\\\"w-4 h-4 rounded-full border border-black/15 flex items-center justify-center opacity-40 mb-1\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-black/40\\\" />\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Minimalist 1:1 Clock */}\\n          <span className=\\\"text-xl font-light tracking-widest text-black/55 tabular-nums\\\">\\n            {currentTime || \'12:00\'}\\n          </span>\\n\\n          <span className=\\\"text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-black/30 font-medium\\\">\\n            Droplet 1:1\\n          </span>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        {/* Dynamic Water Ripples inside the 1:1 window on tap */}\\n        {ripples.map((ripple) => (\\n          <span\\n            key={ripple.id}\\n            className=\\\"pointer-events-none absolute rounded-full border border-black/15 animate-ping opacity-50\\\"\\n            style={{\\n              left: ripple.x - 12,\\n              top: ripple.y - 12,\\n              width: 24,\\n              height: 24,\\n              animationDuration: \'0.85s\',\\n            }}\\n          />\\n        ))}\\n      </div>\\n\\n      {/* Water Taskbar (Static without wild dynamics, resting at bottom of screen) */}\\n      <div className=\\\"absolute bottom-6 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 z-30\\\">\\n        <div className=\\\"water-taskbar\\\">\\n          {/* Main 1:1 Droplet App Icon in Taskbar */}\\n          <div className=\\\"flex flex-col items-center gap-1\\\">\\n            <button\\n              ref={taskbarBeadRef}\\n              type=\\\"button\\\"\\n              aria-label=\\\"Toggle 1:1 Droplet App\\\"\\n              onClick={launchApp}\\n              className=\\\"taskbar-bead group focus:outline-none\\\"\\n              title=\\\"Click to extrude 1:1 Droplet App\\\"\\n            >\\n              {/* Internal micro water highlight */}\\n              <div\\n                className={`w-2 h-2 rounded-full transition-all duration-300 ${\\n                  appStatus !== \'docked\'\\n                    ? \'bg-black/35 scale-110 shadow-sm\'\\n                    : \'bg-black/20 group-hover:bg-black/40\'\\n                }`}\\n              />\\n            </button>\\n\\n            {/* Active app liquid indicator dot */}\\n            <div\\n              className={`w-1.5 h-1 rounded-full transition-all duration-300 ${\\n                appStatus !== \'docked\'\\n                  ? \'bg-black/45 w-2.5 opacity-100\'\\n                  : \'bg-transparent opacity-0\'\\n              }`}\\n            />\\n          </div>\\n\\n          {/* Secondary ambient water bead on the taskbar */}\\n          <div className=\\\"flex flex-col items-center gap-1\\\">\\n            <button\\n              type=\\\"button\\\"\\n              aria-label=\\\"Zen Ripple\\\"\\n              className=\\\"taskbar-bead-secondary focus:outline-none group\\\"\\n              onClick={() => {\\n                if (appStatus === \'floating\') {\\n                  stateRef.current.wobbleVelY -= 8;\\n                  stateRef.current.wobbleVelX += 6;\\n                } else {\\n                  launchApp();\\n                }\\n              }}\\n              title=\\\"Zen ripple\\\"\\n            >\\n              <div className=\\\"w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-black/25 group-hover:bg-black/45 transition-colors\\\" />\\n            </button>\\n            <div className=\\\"w-1.5 h-1\\\" />\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </main>\\n  );\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Implement 1:1 droplet app with calmer restrained deformation and recoil, static water taskbar, and smooth liquid extrusion transition\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/App.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Updating App.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Implement 1:1 app and liquid taskbar extrusion\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\2668\n\2638\001i\024}\023P\312J0\023-3W\a\2665m\277\232\336\251$\306\005\266=\3371i\300[<N\'\306\275\212W\203\236+\275\373W\001\263\3362$\231\005ORC(\216n\236i\247\303\347\313\241\033\302\253\207\v\271Y\031\347\244\336d(\347U\221\216\177\376\020NJ\330\322\022\217\006\bZ\216\311\260\376{^\376\335-!%\362\017\213\351\364\336Ev-:[\233kp\350\360a\313,\024F\324\247ZB\206\364I\216\343\351`\366\225\254\211\365k\347\254H\301\224\246\224l})\334\256\005\254\365_\331\353\250\277\216\226\177\036\366{\332\3156\252\200\204\213\305\016fg\034-\020\326\205@\233\277\344\0346\035%\f\276\025&\322\377]6aI\223\026\277h6f\235\231*\257[{\303\354F7Vs,\337\301%\ts\341\377\240B!\236k:\343Z\240\226\246\234\331\214\360\232Y\310J\242\304\256T\217[WA\234\036\366\320\"M\023\360\n\374\024\317k\036e\375\350\314\226\006\364p\277\032\355\323Z\t\332N\351\341\003\0225\372\026\20314\v\353\231\006\375\016\240\231\034\364\\\266\002\256\377\204\263\226\271\031S\326\364\b1\340|]\265\r\307\0177\334\2672,\366\357\260\370dI\246\230\221\033\023I\027\v\341\303\227Y\005b\354\225\363+\\J\323]\355/\035G\337~d\315k\'Az\003}\211\030^\315\236\377\\ni\277\020\316\024`\266\257/\213\201\357d\370\024\307\341R{d)i\000\177\252\257(\232\310\377\n=\262 \022zz[uSu\364X=U\"\"&\300\202\375\034VJ\372\325K\372\033\347+\347>K\345y{\204\332\252@\375\335\027\003\267~E\244j\341No\221j\016\026\352\320\322\005\361U\244\265T<t_\by8=^\275\332\265\265Q\v1\203\266\350y\'g\261O\035H\346\220fdhC\354f\372\337\302=\240[\023&/g\0047\236\241\211\b5\343sA\300r\367v\326\346\334?\253k\313\034V\2623\021e\337,!\334\v\247\0021\231\021SW\210[\254\231]\024\372\200\374\257^\334?\347\2525\260\275\001\343\325\177pbc\217\305\225\352\374\301\300\355\371\033\260\327\253\317\326\334\f\352\334\bD\036\337\367^`\204:`\204\347\346Sf\003\240\021ueb\341\310\362J\244j\263\331\255\321\234\264\377\220\036\024ypM[\372\362\3300\377\\b]\205#Z\255\020@\362\251vm\257ASc\r\303\310`\277\003\220lEkKyw\265\276\t\274\230\274X<\004\203\325cK \\]\332#\