  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Resolving App Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! Ensuring `dockApp` is declared prior to `launchApp` and included in its dependencies seems to have squashed the TDZ reference issue. My focus has shifted to the `fetch` error in `index.html`. Time to dive into the specifics of that issue!\n\n\n**Addressing Fetch Error**\n\nI believe I\'ve pinpointed the cause of the `fetch` error. It seems like the Chrome extension environment is tripping over attempts to redefine `window.fetch`. I\'m going to integrate a polyfill/shim directly within the `<head>` of `index.html`. This should allow me to capture and re-route the fetch functionality appropriately, circumventing the issue I\'m seeing. I\'m keen to test this out!\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_11498286617473524705"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Add window.fetch getter/setter shim and extension error handler to index.html\",\"EndLine\":6,\"Instruction\":\"Add fetch property shim at top of head\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\" />\\n    <script>\\n      (function() {\\n        try {\\n          var originalFetch = window.fetch;\\n          var currentFetch = originalFetch;\\n          Object.defineProperty(window, \'fetch\', {\\n            get: function() {\\n              return currentFetch;\\n            },\\n            set: function(val) {\\n              currentFetch = val;\\n            },\\n            configurable: true,\\n            enumerable: true\\n          });\\n        } catch (e) {}\\n\\n        window.addEventListener(\'error\', function(e) {\\n          if (e && (e.filename && e.filename.startsWith(\'chrome-extension://\') || (e.message && e.message.includes(\'fetch of #<Window>\')))) {\\n            e.preventDefault();\\n            e.stopImmediatePropagation();\\n          }\\n        }, true);\\n      })();\\n    </script>\\n    <title>Water Droplet</title>\",\"StartLine\":4,\"TargetContent\":\"    <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\" />\\n    <title>Water Droplet</title>\",\"TargetFile\":\"/index.html\",\"toolAction\":\"Updating index.html\",\"toolSummary\":\"Add fetch shim to index.html\"}"
