  planner_response {
    response: "I have fixed the error:\n\n- **Cause**: The browser environment/extension was attempting to assign to `window.fetch`, which only exposed a getter on the global prototype in the preview context, triggering `TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter`.\n- **Solution**: Added a global getter/setter property descriptor on `window` in `index.html` prior to script execution so that external extensions and interceptors can assign to `window.fetch` without throwing, alongside an error guard to prevent extension injection errors from interrupting the applet.\n- **Code Clean-up**: Reordered the callback lifecycle (`dockApp` and `launchApp`) in `src/App.tsx` with proper dependency chaining. Verified with `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passing with zero errors."
    modified_response: "I have fixed the error:\n\n- **Cause**: The browser environment/extension was attempting to assign to `window.fetch`, which only exposed a getter on the global prototype in the preview context, triggering `TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter`.\n- **Solution**: Added a global getter/setter property descriptor on `window` in `index.html` prior to script execution so that external extensions and interceptors can assign to `window.fetch` without throwing, alongside an error guard to prevent extension injection errors from interrupting the applet.\n- **Code Clean-up**: Reordered the callback lifecycle (`dockApp` and `launchApp`) in `src/App.tsx` with proper dependency chaining. Verified with `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` passing with zero errors."
