  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented subtle, high-quality audio triggers synthesized in real-time via the Web Audio API (with zero external audio assets or latency):\n\n- **Launch & Budding**: A gentle rising liquid stretch tone followed by an organic liquid \"pop\" as the droplet emerges from the taskbar.\n- **Neck Snap / Pinch-Off**: A delicate high-frequency micro-bloop the exact instant the liquid bridge detaches.\n- **Velocity-Sensitive Impacts**:\n  - **Floor Landing**: Resonant, deep liquid \"plop\" with volume and pitch scaled to impact velocity.\n  - **Wall Recoil**: Crisp water slap when rebounding off the sides and ceiling.\n  - **Debounced**: Protected with rate limiting to prevent repetitive audio chatter during fast sliding.\n- **Docking & Merging**: A descending liquid immersion sound with a soft settling sub-ripple as the window absorbs back into the taskbar bead.\n- **Window Tap & Ripple**: A crystalline micro-droplet chime when tapping inside the 1:1 window."
    thinking: "**Refining Soundscapes**\n\nI\'ve successfully implemented pure Web Audio API synthesis, eliminating external files and latency. The launch sound now features a rising liquid meniscus stretch and an organic detachment \"bloop.\" For the neck snap sound, I\'m focusing on a high-frequency, delicate micro-bloop at the point of detachment. Volumes are refined to a subtle range of 0.03-0.12, enhancing the delicate nature of the soundscapes.\n\n\n"
