  search_web {
    query: "\"water\" \"drop.mp3\" OR \"drop.wav\" OR \"waterdrop.mp3\" cdn.jsdelivr.net OR unpkg.com"
    summary: "If you are looking to load or reference a water drop or general drop audio asset (`.mp3` or `.wav`) via a content delivery network like **jsDelivr** or **unpkg**, you typically pull them from public npm packages that bundle static assets or sound effects. \n\nBecause npm packages structure their file paths differently, here is how you can target them using jsDelivr or unpkg URL structures:\n\n### 1. Using jsDelivr (`cdn.jsdelivr.net`)\njsDelivr can serve individual files directly from any npm package repository using the `@version` (or `@latest`) specifier:\n```html\n<!-- Generic pattern for an audio file inside an npm package -->\n<audio id=\"waterDrop\" src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/package-name@latest/path/to/drop.mp3\" preload=\"auto\"></audio>\n```\n\n### 2. Using unpkg (`unpkg.com`)\nunpkg operates similarly, mapping directly to files published on npm:\n```html\n<!-- Generic pattern using unpkg -->\n<audio id=\"waterDrop\" src=\"https://unpkg.com/package-name@latest/path/to/drop.mp3\" preload=\"auto\"></audio>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Alternatives & Best Practices for Web Audio\nIf you cannot find a direct standalone audio file hosted reliably via npm for your specific use-case, consider these alternatives:\n\n1. **Host the asset locally or on a cloud bucket:** For sound effects like water drops (`drop.mp3` or `waterdrop.mp3`), keeping the file in your own project\'s `/assets/audio/` directory or uploading it to a dedicated static host/CDN (like AWS S3, Cloudinary, or GitHub Pages) prevents broken links if an npm package gets deprecated or rearranged.\n2. **Programmatic Web Audio (No external file needed):** If you just want a quick interactive \"blob\" or \"plop\" sound without dealing with external MP3/WAV network requests, you can synthesize a water drop sound entirely via the browser\'s native **Web Audio API**:\n   ```javascript\n   function playWaterDrop() {\n       const audioCtx = new (window.AudioContext || window.webkitAudioContext)();\n       const osc = audioCtx.createOscillator();\n       const gain = audioCtx.createGain();\n\n       // Pitch bend down to mimic liquid surface tension / droplet resonance\n       osc.frequency.setValueAtTime(600, audioCtx.currentTime);\n       osc.frequency.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(150, audioCtx.currentTime + 0.1);\n\n       gain.gain.setValueAtTime(0.3, audioCtx.currentTime);\n       gain.gain.exponentialRampToValueAtTime(0.001, audioCtx.currentTime + 0.1);\n\n       osc.connect(gain);\n       gain.connect(audioCtx.destination);\n\n       osc.start();\n       osc.stop(audioCtx.currentTime + 0.1);\n   }\n   ```"
    third_party_config {
      provider: THIRD_PARTY_WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER_GEMINI
    }
    search_type: SEARCH_WEB_TYPE_WEB
  }
}
