    summary: "Your search query targets code repositories, assets, documentation, or lists on GitHub containing references to water-related audio files (`drop.wav`, `drop.mp3`, `drip.wav`, or `splash.wav`). \n\nBecause GitHub does not expose a standard public search results page layout for automated API parsing without authentication, here is a summary of what this search query typically looks for and surfaces across open-source repositories:\n\n### 1. Game Development & Audio Assets\nMany indie games, arcade-style clones (like rain-catcher games), or physics simulations hosted on GitHub store their audio assets in directories like `assets/`, `resources/`, or `res/raw/`. \n* **Examples found in repositories:** \n  * Repositories containing `drop.mp3` or `drop.wav` used as feedback SFX when catching falling items or rain[1].\n  * Physics puzzle games utilizing `splash.wav` or `ripple.wav` for water-impact mechanics[2].\n  * Android applications referencing notification or effect clips (e.g., `res/raw/drop.wav`)[3].\n\n### 2. Documentation and Implementation Guides\nMarkdown files (`.md`) tracking audio pipelines or asset checklists often map out file requirements explicitly. For example:\n* `AUDIO_IMPLEMENTATION.md` files that list fallback placeholder audio files like `splash.wav` (water impact sound) or `launch.wav`[2].\n\n### 3. Machine Learning & Datasets\nAudio recognition, vocal imitation datasets, or sound-classification projects hosted on GitHub often include `.csv` manifests or JSON metadata mapping out audio samples, URLs, or labels matching water drops, drips, and splashes[4].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGAIpD7vZPzFivruiA9iAurni4fTTgSijdtsk9ReeoUdo38AxKUc0FzWid6xbbFE5gPZrgpQg4HOTCrd7gMw0CJpzIZjCp2x9gq23wkLgFd9gSCL-w-6-_YRkQAzanET1_xuZ3WDRRY_26ca3c5_b-YXV5SMA==)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFrP4g1SZoqiVXMtf1ed3wX84XK8AmoG9ipXt7XPECa0alzrFnWEudtPLSxl0NGfcrEbdDKaUcb7zG3VfhY8Sa_2HOpAlU9d_WOFckYHXAz5HIBzIRPYgxgTMMGGxFLKyyC8f-V8NZfMdlw5Gy7weX5fz_T3xgveIYdHMpZ_CjM1iLCbX7V2g==)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF1ZoWoDF2IC4P1KobHTJt21wfHWbV8C5pVOfeARPcndOja2MaennOrT_ejjWtmKOTqsGsgFrkKqss0xogo8dv14DLLdE6RW4mBd_yvfQIXYuD3hiAiNaavgB6a37eql2HWeC4jcVYmsrKqpu7N)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG6ah2HAUy-VZGXMOs7eVyVyFmFRXrCcP6yLcIJNjzGLujoJVJFCn6Uv8ImYc7Q9VoxfTpvLF2VHeB_ERclql86fYzDLq_BfpNXtsG0G3S9HDmkX3CX94X9ei_h1DqxUWfZDbLC9AalxSmSTpBtjkdJzLyG8D6SMXYzNfcvux9ivRJZbkfZU0q38bHZVbJqL2qdYvaVS3TssnkK)"
