  planner_response {
    response: "I have implemented the **vapor trail effect** behind high-speed droplets:\n\n- **High-Velocity Detection**: Whenever a droplet is thrown or rebounds at high speeds (`> 330 px/s`), a stream of vapor particles is continuously generated along the flight path behind the droplet.\n- **Shrinking & Fading Circles**: Each particle starts with a radius proportional to the droplet\'s size and speed, then shrinks smoothly towards zero while its opacity fades over a ~0.45s lifespan.\n- **Aesthetic**:\n  - Rendered on a dedicated SVG layer beneath the windows (`z-5`).\n  - Styled with a soft radial mist gradient (`#vaporDropGrad`) featuring water condensation tones and a delicate Gaussian blur (`#vaporSoftBlur`).\n- **60\342\200\223120 FPS Performance**: Powered by a 75-circle pre-allocated object pool directly synchronized within the requestAnimationFrame physics loop, ensuring zero React re-render overhead or garbage collection pauses."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Implemented Effects**\n\nI\'ve been going over the \"vapor trail\" effect implementation. I\'m focusing on the shrinking, fading SVG circles that trail the droplets at high speed. It\'s about getting the animation just right to look believable. The challenge now is fine-tuning the transparency and timing so it doesn\'t look clunky. I think I\'m close to a good iteration, I\'ll review again later.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have implemented the **vapor trail effect** behind high-speed droplets:\n\n- **High-Velocity Detection**: Whenever a droplet is thrown or rebounds at high speeds (`> 330 px/s`), a stream of vapor particles is continuously generated along the flight path behind the droplet.\n- **Shrinking & Fading Circles**: Each particle starts with a radius proportional to the droplet\'s size and speed, then shrinks smoothly towards zero while its opacity fades over a ~0.45s lifespan.\n- **Aesthetic**:\n  - Rendered on a dedicated SVG layer beneath the windows (`z-5`).\n  - Styled with a soft radial mist gradient (`#vaporDropGrad`) featuring water condensation tones and a delicate Gaussian blur (`#vaporSoftBlur`).\n- **60\342\200\223120 FPS Performance**: Powered by a 75-circle pre-allocated object pool directly synchronized within the requestAnimationFrame physics loop, ensuring zero React re-render overhead or garbage collection pauses."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 928262781
