  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **User Request**: Implement a \"fade to nothing\" animation when a droplet reaches a very small scale, simulating evaporation rather than just disappearing.\n   - **Scope Boundaries**: Pure white background (`#ffffff`), 1:1 water droplet app windows, static taskbar at the bottom, zero unnecessary HUD or UI clutter.\n   - **Target Context**:\n     - Dev App URL: `https://ais-dev-vtfybaf4evvm7vnogeflk3-792758671607.europe-west2.run.app`\n     - Applet ID: `61f3708d-4618-4a1d-acba-4748a372a1dd`\n     - Port: 3000\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed in earlier turns**:\n     - Realistic water droplet CSS with inner/outer shadows and glare highlights (`src/index.css`).\n     - Real recorded water sound effects in `public/sounds/*.mp3` and `src/soundAssets.ts` (base64 DataURIs decoded into Web Audio API `AudioBuffer`s in `src/audio.ts`).\n     - Multi-droplet window spawning from the taskbar, bounce vs. merge collision physics, and vapor trail particles at high speeds (`src/App.tsx`).\n     - Extended `DropletStatus` to include `\'evaporating\'` and added `opacity`, `evaporateStartTime`, `evaporateDuration`, `evaporateStartScale` to `DropletState` interface and `spawnDroplet` initialization in `/src/App.tsx`.\n   - **In Progress (Half-finished edit in `/src/App.tsx`)**:\n     - Need to implement the `\'evaporating\'` lifecycle handling in the physics loop in `src/App.tsx`:\n       1. Transitioning into `\'evaporating\'` when:\n          - A droplet is absorbed during inter-droplet merge (currently `absorbed.status = \'merged_out\'`).\n          - A droplet reaches a small scale threshold (e.g. `scale < 0.28`).\n          - A droplet finishes docking into the taskbar (`progress >= 1` in docking transition).\n       2. Executing the evaporation animation in the RAF loop:\n          - Exponential decay of scale to 0: `scale = evaporateStartScale * Math.pow(1 - progress, 2)`.\n          - Smooth opacity decay: `opacity = Math.pow(1 - progress, 1.4)`.\n          - Upward wisp drift and emitting 2-3 delicate mist vapor puffs via `vaporParticlesRef`.\n          - Updating `el.style.opacity = (drop.status === \'evaporating\' ? drop.opacity : 1).toFixed(3)` and `el.style.pointerEvents`.\n          - Marking `drop.status = \'merged_out\'` and pushing to `pendingRemovals` once `progress >= 1`.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - `DropletState` now contains `opacity`, `evaporateStartTime`, `evaporateDuration`, `evaporateStartScale`.\n   - Card DOM elements are tracked in `cardElementsRef = useRef<Map<string, HTMLDivElement>>(new Map())`.\n   - Updating `el.style.opacity` dynamically is safe and performant because `.card` in `src/index.css` has `will-change: transform, border-radius, opacity`.\n   - Merges previously immediately removed the absorbed droplet; by giving the absorbed droplet a short `evaporateDuration = 0.32s` with drift into the dominant droplet, it creates a seamless organic dissolution.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Error 1**: `TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter` from extension/preview script `200.js`.\n     - *Fix*: Defined a property descriptor on `window` in `index.html` with both getter and setter before any scripts execute.\n   - **Error 2**: `Expected corresponding JSX closing tag for \'filter\'` in `App.tsx` due to duplicate closing tag on `<feDropShadow ... />`.\n     - *Fix*: Removed duplicate `</feDropShadow>` in `replace_file_content`.\n   - **Error 3**: `tsc --noEmit` error `Type \'AudioBuffer | undefined\' is not assignable to type \'AudioBuffer\'`.\n     - *Fix*: Added proper type assertion and check `if (loaded) buffer = loaded;` in `src/audio.ts`.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - `src/App.tsx` has already had `DropletStatus` and `newDrop` updated.\n   - Next edits must update the loop logic and DOM styling in `src/App.tsx`.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. **Edit `src/App.tsx`**:\n      - In `loop`:\n        - In `drop.status === \'docking\'`: When `progress >= 1`, instead of immediate `drop.status = \'merged_out\'`, trigger:\n          ```ts\n          drop.status = \'evaporating\';\n          drop.evaporateStartTime = timestamp;\n          drop.evaporateDuration = 0.28;\n          drop.evaporateStartScale = drop.scale;\n          playMergeSound();\n          ```\n        - In `drop.status === \'floating\'`: Add small scale check:\n          ```ts\n          if (drop.scale < 0.28) {\n            drop.status = \'evaporating\';\n            drop.evaporateStartTime = timestamp;\n            drop.evaporateDuration = 0.38;\n            drop.evaporateStartScale = drop.scale;\n            playRippleSound();\n          }\n          ```\n        - Add branch `else if (drop.status === \'evaporating\')`:\n          Compute `elapsed` and `progress`.\n          Calculate `drop.scale = drop.evaporateStartScale * Math.pow(1 - progress, 2)`.\n          Calculate `drop.opacity = Math.pow(1 - progress, 1.4)`.\n          Drift gently `drop.x += drop.vx * dt`, `drop.y += (drop.vy - 30) * dt`.\n          Emit tiny mist wisps into `vaporParticlesRef`.\n          When `progress >= 1`, mark `drop.status = \'merged_out\'` and `pendingRemovals.push(drop.id)`.\n        - In inter-droplet merge collision:\n          Instead of `absorbed.status = \'merged_out\'`, set:\n          ```ts\n          absorbed.status = \'evaporating\';\n          absorbed.evaporateStartTime = timestamp;\n          absorbed.evaporateDuration = 0.35;\n          absorbed.evaporateStartScale = absorbed.scale;\n          absorbed.isDragging = false;\n          absorbed.vx = (dominant.x - absorbed.x) * 3;\n          absorbed.vy = (dominant.y - absorbed.y) * 3;\n          ```\n        - In DOM rendering loop:\n          Set `el.style.opacity = (drop.status === \'evaporating\' ? drop.opacity : 1).toFixed(3);`\n          Set `el.style.pointerEvents = drop.status === \'evaporating\' ? \'none\' : \'auto\';`\n   2. **Verify**:\n      - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` together to verify 0 build and typing errors.\n      - Restart dev server with `restart_dev_server`.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - Strictly retain the pure white background with zero UI or HUD.\n   - Preserve all real recorded water sounds in `src/audio.ts`.\n   - Maintain 60-120fps direct RAF performance with no per-frame React re-renders.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 279
    render_latest_checkpoint: true
    total_subagent_count: 0
    captured_user_requests {
      text: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
