    thinking: "**Examining Card Component**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `card` component, specifically lines 905-940, to observe its rendering process. I\'ve found an opportunity to integrate a context menu using `onContextMenu` that will call `handleEvaporate(item.id)` to prevent the default action.\n\n\n**Refining Evaporation Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the evaporation logic for the droplets. I\'ve added double-click functionality to `.minimize-bead` to call `handleEvaporate`, preventing event propagation. Normal clicks will now `dockDroplet(item.id)` to taskbar. I\'ve implemented automatic evaporation if the droplet scale drops below 0.28, and a fade animation for merges. I\'m also adding right-click and double-click evaporation triggers. Finally, I\'m reviewing code adjustments to `src/App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Evaporation States**\n\nI\'m now implementing distinct evaporation states. I\'ve defined `evaporateStartTime`, `evaporateDuration`, and `evaporateStartScale` to track the process. I\'m also slowing down the x velocity, and adding upward drift upon evaporation initiation. I\'ve updated the loop to handle an \'evaporating\' status and added an animation for water vaporization. The docking status will transition to the evaporating status when merging.\n\n\n**Calculating Evaporation Effects**\n\nI\'m now calculating the visual effects for the evaporation process using `drop.evaporateDuration` and an elapsed time variable to track progress. I\'m applying a cubic shrink curve and exponential opacity fade. I\'ve incorporated soft thermal mist ascent and horizontal velocity dampening. I\'m also emitting mist vapor particles that dissipate, and I\'m using `Math.random` to vary their appearance.\n\n\n**Adjusting Mist Properties**\n\nI\'m now refining the properties of the thermal mist particles emitted during the evaporation. I\'ve been setting the initial radius, current radius, opacity, life, and max life for each particle. The opacity is randomized to ensure variation, and I\'ve also established a maximum lifespan for the particle. I\'ve included a check to change the status of drops if their scale is less than 0.28, which then triggers evaporation. Finally, I\'ve adjusted the code to change the status of merged drops to `merged_out`.\n\n\n**Implementing Evaporation Transition**\n\nI\'m now incorporating a smooth evaporation transition for absorbed droplets. I\'ve set the absorbed droplet\'s status to \'evaporating\' upon absorption and established the evaporation start time and duration, along with the starting scale. I\'m adjusting its velocity vector and also disabling the dragging capability. In the DOM styling loop, I am also updating the scale limits to ensure the droplet scales down in evaporation. The scale will have a min of 0.001 during evaporation. I\'m adjusting its velocity vector for a smooth transition. The z-index and opacity are also adjusted during the evaporation process.\n\n\n"
