  planner_response {
    response: "### Droplet Evaporation (\"Fade to Nothing\") Implementation\n\n- **Scale & Opacity Vaporization Curve**: When a droplet reaches a small scale (`scale < 0.28`), docks into the taskbar, is absorbed during coalescence, or is triggered via right-click/double-click, it enters the `evaporating` state. Its scale decays smoothly to zero via a non-linear exponential curve (`Math.pow(1 - progress, 2.2)`) while its opacity dissolves to complete transparency (`Math.pow(1 - progress, 1.4)`).\n- **Physical Thermal Ascent & Mist Dispersion**: During evaporation, the droplet undergoes a gentle upward thermal drift while releasing soft micro-mist vapor particles that disperse and fade naturally into the air.\n- **Natural Collision Dissolution**: Absorbed droplets in mergers no longer vanish instantaneously; they now fluidly evaporate into the absorbing droplet before being cleaned up from active state."
