  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Surface Tension**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a \"Surface Tension\" toggle. My latest idea is that enabling it would cause nearby droplets to subtly attract and merge, mimicking real-world surface tension. I\'m imagining a gradual, realistic pull, instead of instant snapping.\n\n\n**Analyzing Droplet Behavior**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on how to handle the behavior of water droplets, specifically when they are separated. I need to figure out how to best create a visual for them being separate.\n\n\n**Integrating Surface Tension**\n\nI\'ve decided on the \"Surface Tension\" toggle\'s placement: it\'ll live on the liquid taskbar, styled as a water bead. When active, it will have a meniscus glow or subtle droplet attraction indicator, and will play a soft ripple sound. This mimics the other beads in style and feel. I\'m focusing now on its active/inactive state visual cues.\n\n\n"
