  planner_response {
    response: "### Surface Tension Setting Implementation\n\n- **Capillary Attraction Physics**: When Surface Tension is enabled, separated droplets within capillary reach (`~2.85\303\227` combined radii) naturally exert an attractive pull on one another. The pull scales non-linearly (`proximity^1.35`), causing nearby droplets to gently drift, slide across surfaces, and accelerate together.\n- **Meniscus Stretch Pre-Coalescence**: As droplets draw close under mutual attraction, they viscoelastic-stretch along their angle of approach before surface tension snaps them together into a single merged droplet with the recorded water merge sound.\n- **Liquid Taskbar Toggle**: Added a dedicated water bead on the bottom taskbar with twin coalescing micro-droplets and an illuminated active indicator dot. Clicking it toggles the setting with tactile water ripple audio feedback. When disabled, droplets bounce off one another elastically without pulling together."
