  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Splash Particles**\n\nI\'ve got the SVG circle pool for vapor particles figured out. Now, I\'m diving into designing the splash particles. My current focus is to introduce a radial burst of tiny, white, semi-transparent particles around the base of the droplet. This will simulate a splash effect when it impacts the screen edges or floor. Next up: designing the `SplashParticle` class.\n\n\n**Defining Particle Properties**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously defining the `SplashParticle` interface, carefully enumerating the necessary properties like position, velocity, radii, opacity, and lifespan. I\'m focusing on the behavior of real water splashes: the point of impact and how the particles should burst from the droplet and from the impact. I\'ve broken down the particle burst to reflect various impact scenarios. I am now focused on defining splash angle theta and burst velocities for the splashes.\n\n\n**Calculating Splash Angles**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about splash angles, relative to the normal. I am defining a good range of angles from $-75^\\circ$ to $+75^\\circ$ (relative to normal $(1, 0)$) for a typical impact. I\'m also now considering right wall impacts, where angles range from $105^\\circ$ to $255^\\circ$ relative to normal $(-1, 0)$, and ceiling impacts, with angles from $15^\\circ$ to $165^\\circ$.\n\n\n"
