  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Splash Effect**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on line 310 in the `loop` function. It looks like a good spot to define `triggerSplash`. This function will create a radial burst of small, white, semi-transparent splash particles around a droplet\'s impact point. I\'m focusing on the impact event and the visual effect generated.\n\n\n**Refining Splash Particle Generation**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into how the splash particles themselves are created, specifically within the loop. The `count` calculation seems pivotal, directly influencing the number of particles generated based on impact speed and scale. The radial spray pattern is shaping up nicely, and the ejection velocity calculations are more robust now, I feel. The base radius and maximum life for each particle are coming into focus, too.\n\n\n"
