  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing SVG Rendering**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how to render an SVG layer, specifically the \"Vapor Trail\" and \"Splash Particles\" elements within a JSX context. I\'m exploring the use of `<svg>` tags for this purpose, with considerations for styling like `className`, positioning with `absolute` and `inset-0`, and handling pointer events via `pointer-events-none`. I\'m especially interested in the implications of `overflow-hidden` and `z-8` for layering.\n\n\n**Implementing SVG Enhancements**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the SVG elements. I am adding a radial gradient and drop shadow filter to the splash particles for visual depth. I\'m using a `defs` block within the SVG to define these reusable components. The radial gradient (`splashDropGrad`) is using multiple stop colors with varying opacities to simulate light effects.\n\n\n"
