  planner_response {
    response: "### Radial Impact Splash Particles Implementation\n\n- **Radial Burst on Collision**: When a droplet impacts the screen floor or any screen edge (left wall, right wall, or ceiling), a radial burst of 9\342\200\22326 tiny, semi-transparent white water droplets erupts from the contact point around the base of the droplet.\n- **Ballistic Trajectories & Dispersion**: Ejected splash particles follow natural ballistic parabolic arcs influenced by gravity (`vy += GRAVITY * 0.72 * dt`) and air drag, spreading in an outward fan oriented along the impact surface normal.\n- **Glassy Water Droplet Aesthetics**: Rendered with translucent white radial gradients, delicate specular highlights, and soft refraction drop-shadows that remain crisp and legible against the pure white canvas.\n- **Dynamic Dissipation & Pooling**: Splash particles shrink and fade exponentially over their lifetime (`~0.3\342\200\2230.5s`) using a pre-allocated SVG circle pool driven directly within the 60\342\200\223120fps physics loop with zero React re-render overhead."
