  planner_response {
    response: "### Droplet Surface Ripple Animation on Collisions\n\n- **Screen Edge Collision Propagation**: When a droplet impacts the floor, ceiling, left wall, or right wall, a subtle water surface ripple animation (`.water-surface-ripple`) propagates outward across the droplet\'s meniscus from the exact point of impact (bottom, top, left, or right surface edge).\n- **Inter-Droplet Collision Waves**: During droplet collisions\342\200\224both high-velocity elastic rebounds and surface-tension coalescence merges\342\200\224surface ripples originate at the mutual contact interface vector and sweep across each colliding droplet.\n- **Translucent Wave Ring Aesthetics**: Styled with high-contrast white refractive crests (`rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95)` with `box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8)`) and subtle dark fluid troughs (`inset 0 0 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)`) that expand smoothly (`scale(0.18)` to `scale(5.2)`) and fade within the droplet\'s boundary.\n- **Throttling & Direct DOM Animation**: Surface ripples are throttled per droplet during rapid collisions to prevent wave stacking, running directly on the GPU without triggering React re-renders in the physics loop."
    modified_response: "### Droplet Surface Ripple Animation on Collisions\n\n- **Screen Edge Collision Propagation**: When a droplet impacts the floor, ceiling, left wall, or right wall, a subtle water surface ripple animation (`.water-surface-ripple`) propagates outward across the droplet\'s meniscus from the exact point of impact (bottom, top, left, or right surface edge).\n- **Inter-Droplet Collision Waves**: During droplet collisions\342\200\224both high-velocity elastic rebounds and surface-tension coalescence merges\342\200\224surface ripples originate at the mutual contact interface vector and sweep across each colliding droplet.\n- **Translucent Wave Ring Aesthetics**: Styled with high-contrast white refractive crests (`rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95)` with `box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8)`) and subtle dark fluid troughs (`inset 0 0 5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)`) that expand smoothly (`scale(0.18)` to `scale(5.2)`) and fade within the droplet\'s boundary.\n- **Throttling & Direct DOM Animation**: Surface ripples are throttled per droplet during rapid collisions to prevent wave stacking, running directly on the GPU without triggering React re-renders in the physics loop."
