  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Drop Physics**\n\nI\'ve been examining the code, specifically lines 548-555, focusing on the physics of the \"drop\" object. I\'m looking at how gravity and air resistance are applied to its velocity changes over time. I am interested in understanding how those factors combine to impact the object\'s movement.\n\n\n**Investigating Bounce Dynamics**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the floor collision section, specifically how the code calculates and applies the impact speed. The interactions between `impactSpeed`, `squashPower`, and the wobble velocities are interesting. I\'m also examining the implications of `BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_BOTTOM` on the drop\'s subsequent vertical velocity. The splash particles and surface ripple triggers are also important aspects to consider.\n\n\n**Exploring Ceiling Collisions**\n\nI\'m now diving into the code related to ceiling collisions, specifically the handling of impact speed and the triggering of effects. I find the conditional sound triggering based on impactSpeed interesting, alongside how the code calculates the squashPower, which affects wobble velocities. Furthermore, I\'m examining the generation of the radial splash particles and surface ripples upon ceiling impact.\n\n\n**Examining Wall Interactions**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the code for both left wall and right wall collisions. Specifically, I\'m examining how the `impactSpeed` affects sound playback and the application of `squashPower` to wobble velocities. I\'m also observing how the system responds if gravity is zero, or negative. I find the conditional logic for the radial splash particle generation crucial for understanding visual feedback. Furthermore, the `BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_WALL` is interesting.\n\n\n**Analyzing Wall Reactions**\n\nI am now closely examining the conditional logic for how the system responds if gravityX is zero or negative when the drop interacts with walls, especially how horizontal velocity and vertical velocities are handled in that specific scenario. I\'m also now analyzing the impact of `BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_WALL` on the object\'s horizontal motion, along with the radial splash particle generation on the right side screen impact.\n\n\n**Assessing Tilt Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating device orientation into the model. I\'ve noted how subtle acceleration affects the droplets, and I\'m looking at implementing a visual cue to show that the tilt is active. I\'m also examining how the orientation listener integrates with the user experience. The system requests permission, seamlessly, upon the user\'s first gesture!\n\n\n"
