  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Orientation Detection**\n\nI\'m focusing on incorporating `orientationRef` and the `useEffect` hook for device orientation listening directly into `src/App.tsx`. I\'m double-checking the implementation of the effect, specifically the device orientation state in the reference, to ensure it\'s functioning as intended.\n\n\n**Refining Orientation Listener**\n\nI\'ve refined the device orientation listener within the `useEffect` hook, now clamping the tilt angles for more natural handling, specifically from -60 to 60 for gamma, and -90 to 90 for beta. I\'m also converting these angles to radians, in preparation for the upcoming RAF physics loop. This should ensure smooth and predictable tilt responses.\n\n\n**Attaching Device Orientation**\n\nI\'m now attaching the device orientation event listener. I\'ve integrated `tiltX` and `tiltY` calculations using `Math.sin` on the `gammaRad` and `betaRad` values, updating `orientationRef` with these target values and setting `hasSensor` to true. I\'ve also added conditional checks for permission requests, ensuring the listener attaches only when granted or when the event is supported.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_3740016144780629873"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Add orientationRef and device orientation listener effect in App.tsx\",\"EndLine\":164,\"Instruction\":\"Add orientationRef and device orientation listener effect right after live clock\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"  // Live clock\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const updateTime = () => {\\n      const d = new Date();\\n      setCurrentTime(d.toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: \'2-digit\', minute: \'2-digit\' }));\\n    };\\n    updateTime();\\n    const interval = setInterval(updateTime, 1000);\\n    return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Device orientation state in ref for 60-120fps RAF physics loop\\n  const orientationRef = useRef<{\\n    hasSensor: boolean;\\n    targetX: number;\\n    targetY: number;\\n    currentX: number;\\n    currentY: number;\\n  }>({\\n    hasSensor: false,\\n    targetX: 0,\\n    targetY: 1, // default vertical downward gravity\\n    currentX: 0,\\n    currentY: 1,\\n  });\\n\\n  // Device orientation listener with iOS permission support and smooth tilt filtering\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    let isMounted = true;\\n\\n    const handleOrientation = (e: DeviceOrientationEvent) => {\\n      if (e.gamma === null && e.beta === null) return;\\n\\n      const gamma = e.gamma ?? 0; // -90 to 90 (left to right tilt)\\n      const beta = e.beta ?? 0;   // -180 to 180 (front to back tilt)\\n\\n      // Clamp tilt angles to natural handling range\\n      const clampedGamma = Math.max(-60, Math.min(60, gamma));\\n      const clampedBeta = Math.max(-90, Math.min(90, beta));\\n\\n      const gammaRad = (clampedGamma * Math.PI) / 180;\\n      const betaRad = (clampedBeta * Math.PI) / 180;\\n\\n      // Subtle directional tilt acceleration vector\\n      const tiltX = Math.sin(gammaRad);\\n      const tiltY = Math.sin(betaRad);\\n\\n      orientationRef.current.hasSensor = true;\\n      orientationRef.current.targetX = tiltX;\\n      orientationRef.current.targetY = tiltY;\\n    };\\n\\n    const requestAndAttach = () => {\\n      if (\\n        typeof DeviceOrientationEvent !== \'undefined\' &&\\n        typeof (DeviceOrientationEvent as unknown as { requestPermission?: () => Promise<string> }).requestPermission === \'function\'\\n      ) {\\n        (DeviceOrientationEvent as unknown as { requestPermission: () => Promise<string> })\\n          .requestPermission()\\n          .then((res: string) => {\\n            if (res === \'granted\' && isMounted) {\\n              window.addEventListener(\'deviceorientation\', handleOrientation, true);\\n            }\\n          })\\n          .catch(() => {});\\n      } else if (typeof window !== \'undefined\' && \'DeviceOrientationEvent\' in window) {\\n        window.addEventListener(\'deviceorientation\', handleOrientation, true);\\n      }\\n    };\\n\\n    requestAndAttach();\\n\\n    // Re-check on first user gesture for browsers requiring user gesture (e.g. iOS Safari)\\n    const handleGesture = () => {\\n      requestAndAttach();\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'pointerdown\', handleGesture);\\n    };\\n    window.addEventListener(\'pointerdown\', handleGesture, { once: true });\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      isMounted = false;\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'deviceorientation\', handleOrientation, true);\\n      window.removeEventListener(\'pointerdown\', handleGesture);\\n    };\\n  }, []);\",\"StartLine\":154,\"TargetContent\":\"  // Live clock\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const updateTime = () => {\\n      const d = new Date();\\n      setCurrentTime(d.toLocaleTimeString([], { hour: \'2-digit\', minute: \'2-digit\' }));\\n    };\\n    updateTime();\\n    const interval = setInterval(updateTime, 1000);\\n    return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n  }, []);\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/App.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Adding device orientation listener effect\",\"toolSummary\":\"Add orientation listener to App.tsx\"}"
