e `impactSpeed` threshold and how it triggers impact effects like sounds, particles, and ripples. The relationship between `squashPower` and wobble velocity intrigues me, I\'m also scrutinizing the application of `BOUNCE_RESTITUTION_WALL` and the conditions leading to complete horizontal stop.\n\n\n**Examining Right Wall Impact**\n\nI\'m now investigating the right wall collision scenario. I\'ve focused on the section from lines 852 onwards. I\'m noting that the impact speed dictates the sound, particle effects, and wobble. The `triggerSplash` function, and `triggerDropletRipple` intrigues me, especially considering the direction from which the effects originate. I\'m scrutinizing how the restitution constant and gravity are affecting the droplet\'s behavior after impact. I\'m focusing on the interplay of variables such as `squashPower` to determine the subsequent velocities.\n\n\n"
